    │   │
    │   │   Overall Direction:
    │   │   Revtek should prioritize refined performance over visual excess.
    │   │   The visual identity should feel engineered, intentional,
    │   │   modern, and premium rather than flashy or heavily decorated.
    │   │
    │   │   Avoid:
    │   │   ├── Excessive visual effects
    │   │   ├── Overuse of gradients
    │   │   ├── Excessive text
    │   │   ├── Generic luxury aesthetics
    │   │   ├── Excessive racing graphics
    │   │   ├── Overly aggressive tuning-shop visuals
    │   │   ├── Random decorative elements
    │   │   ├── Heavy carbon-fibre textures
    │   │   ├── Excessive neon / accent colors
    │   │   └── Mixing unrelated visual styles
    │   │
    │   │
    │   ├── Layout & Composition
    │   │   ├── Photography-first
    │   │   ├── Strong negative space
    │   │   ├── Clear visual hierarchy
    │   │   ├── Consistent alignment
    │   │   ├── Structured grid
    │   │   └── One primary message per visual
    │   │
    │   │   Recommended hierarchy:
    │   │   1. Vehicle / Product
    │   │   2. Project / Product Name
    │   │   3. Key Message
    │   │   4. Supporting Information
    │   │   5. Brand / CTA
